o wording that carries character. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Ignore the sentence and invent a more exciting event.","Say the writing is good without naming any words.","A narrator and a character are not automatically the same person.","Point to exact words in the sentence that show character and say what they do."],"question":"Read: \"At dawn, Mina whispered to her goat as frost glittered on the fence.\" Which choice best uses character from this lesson?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"The correct statement applies the language skill with textual evidence. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Copy a model sentence from another story unchanged.","Name setting and point to the words or events without linking it to any words in the text.","The koala is the character;","A narrator and a character are not automatically the same person."],"question":"Which statement correctly applies the lesson idea about character?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Start from a specific textual clue, then explain its effect. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Locate a specific word, phrase or structural clue before deciding.","Guess from the title alone with no textual clue.","Copy a model sentence from another story unchanged.","Lengthen the answer with adjectives while keeping the same idea."],"question":"In a new text, what should you do first to analyse setting and point to the words or events?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Repair means fixing meaning or evidence, not padding. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Change the inaccurate idea or missing evidence, not only the length.","Add adjectives without fixing the wrong idea.","Make the answer longer while keeping the same mistake.","Delete the evidence that disagreed with your first guess."],"question":"Which revision actually improves meaning for character?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Accurate transfer needs fresh material with an explained language choice. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Change fonts and claim the work is new.","A narrator and a character are not automatically the same person.","Use a fresh sentence or text and explain one precise choice about character.","Retype the worked model as the final answer."],"question":"Which response shows accurate use of character on fresh material?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Accept original work about character with a specific supporting detail. Reject copied model wording with no new material.","question":"Produce a fresh example demonstrating character on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.","sample_answer":"Sample: original example using character on new material; names a specific word, source or choice and explains its effect.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful correction changes the inaccurate idea or method and explains why.","marking_guide":"Accept a misconception, a correction, and a purpose-linked reason for character. Reject corrections that do not change the inaccurate idea.","question":"Name one likely error with character, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.","sample_answer":"Sample error: A narrator and a character are not automatically the same person.. Correction: The koala is the character; it may need water or cooler weather.. Why it helps the audience is stated.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Submit your original independent work and your brief explanation of the key choices you made.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-eng-y3-w02-l1","sort_a